course: dictionary
lesson: 14734
title: Prohibition: the word for "not allowed"
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A prohibition is a rule that says something is not allowed. Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «There is a prohibition on running by the pool.» The clue is the word on: the rule stops people from running there. So a prohibition is a ban.
explain: You often see prohibitions on signs. A red circle with a line through it usually shows a prohibition, such as a no-entry sign or a no-smoking sign. «The sign on the door is a prohibition: no entry.» Quick check: swap in your meaning, "The sign on the door is a rule: no entry", and it still makes sense.
explain: In history, Prohibition was a special time in the United States. It was the time when making and selling alcohol was against the law. «In the history lesson, we learned about Prohibition.» Here the word starts with a capital letter because it names one period of history.
fact: A prohibition is a rule or law that says something is not allowed.
fact: Prohibition is the act of banning something.
fact: «Prohibition» means a ban, so a prohibition on running means running is banned.
fact: In the United States, Prohibition was the time from 1920 to 1933 when making and selling alcohol was against the law.
fact: Signs often show prohibitions with a red circle and a line through a picture, such as a no-dogs sign.
exercise: «There is a prohibition on running by the pool.» What does prohibition mean here? | *A rule that says running is not allowed | A kind of fast bicycle | A prize for the fastest runner | A place to buy a drink
exercise: Which of these is a prohibition? | A sunny day at the beach | A football match | A birthday cake | *A no-entry sign
exercise: «Prohibition» in US history was a time when making and selling alcohol was against the law. What was banned? | *Making and selling alcohol | Wearing hats in school | Playing football in the street | Eating ice cream
test: «Mum read the sign: a prohibition on phones in class.» What does this mean? | Phones must be charged in class | Phones are a gift for everyone | Phones are on sale today | *Phones are not allowed in class
test: In formal writing, «a prohibition on» means… | *A ban on | A reward for | A party for | A map of
exam: Which sentence shows a prohibition? | *No dogs are allowed in the park | The shop is open until six | We can have ice cream today | The bus is late
